From 8d3e5e6fe6d0be5634b28788abf5685d571b13a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:00:12 -0500
Subject: Bluetooth: hci_core: Don't fail removing a monitor unknown to the controller
Git-commit: 8d3e5e6fe6d0be5634b28788abf5685d571b13a4
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc5
References: git-fixes

hci_remove_adv_monitor() frees the monitor when the controller has no
matching handle for it but still returned -ENOENT, so callers took it for
a failure of a monitor that is gone, and hci_remove_all_adv_monitor()
stopped at the first one leaving the others behind. Return success since
the monitor was removed.

Found by the sashiko.dev review of the previous revision of this series.

Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Link: https://sashiko.dev/#/patchset/20261117185737.3758255-1-luiz.dentz%40gmail.com
Fixes: 7cf5c2978f23 ("Bluetooth: hci_sync: Refactor remove Adv Monitor")
Assisted-by: OpenCode:claude-fable-5.2
Signed-off-by: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 net/bluetooth/hci_core.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
index c7310fcb58b3..255005916f37 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
@@ -2039,7 +2039,10 @@ static int hci_remove_adv_monitor(struct hci_dev *hdev,
 	hci_free_adv_monitor(hdev, monitor);
 	hci_dev_unlock(hdev);
 
-	return status;
+	/* The monitor is gone, not having been known by the controller is not
+	 * an error for the caller.
+	 */
+	return status == -ENOENT ? 0 : status;
 }
 
 /* This function requires the caller holds hci_req_sync_lock */
